  - title: The name on the stall
    number: 8
    heartsNeeded: 8
    path: 0
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - 'I''ve been offered a spot in the plaza. A stall. My old sign is still in the attic: ''Kowalczyk Flowers''.'
    - I could open it again. Your flowers, my know-how. 'Kowalczyk & Farm'. My knees might last a season or two.
    - Or I could give it all to Bea. The sign, the rules, the secrets. She'd enter the Bloom Show under my name, and I'd watch from the bench with a flask.
    - You're the grower, petal. You decide.
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 1
      optionA: Reopen the stall
      replyA:
      - Then it's back to five in the morning! Oh, my knees are going to have words with me.
      - Bring me everything that blooms, petal. And tell the roses they look wonderful. Every day.
      flagsA:
      - ada_stall_open
      optionB: Pass it to Bea
      replyB:
      - Bea, then. She's got the hands for it, and the patience. And young knees.
      - I'll teach her the rules tonight. All of them. Even the one about Fridays, which isn't really a rule. I just like Fridays off.
      flagsB:
      - ada_passed_stall
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: Kowalczyk & Farm
    number: 9
    heartsNeeded: 9
    path: 1
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - 'First Saturday: sold out by eleven. Second Saturday: sold out by ten. Rosa says I''m stealing her customers. I''m sharing them.'
    - 'And the Bloom Show! My sweet peas: a blue ribbon. The tower''s silk roses: nothing. One of the judges sniffed them and made a face.'
    - My knees hurt. My hands smell of earth. I haven't been this happy since the fountain.
    happy: 1
    ask:
